      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEvery test must explicitly separate its Given, When, and Then phases with comments.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat The Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Testing\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; Foundation-service tests visibly separate their setup, execution and assertion phases with given, when and then comments. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/2.%20Services/2.1%20Foundations/2.1%20Foundations.md#213120-testing-structural-validations\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003Cbr\u003E\u0026ldquo;Unit Tests\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; The REST API unit-test examples use the same Given, When and Then phase markers. The analyser enforces this repeated Standard testing convention. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/3.%20Exposers/3.1%20Communication%20Protocols/3.1.1%20RESTful%20APIs/3.1.1%20RESTful%20APIs.md#31150-unit-tests\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGiven, When, and Then comments expose the behavioural structure of a test without explaining implementation trivia. They make preconditions, the single action, and assertions immediately distinguishable and reveal tests that perform several behaviours at once.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STXTEST005: Every test must explicitly separate its Given, When, and Then phases with comments.\u003C/span\u003E\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E]\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Easync\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldAddStudent\u003C/span\u003E()\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E student = \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ECreateStudent\u003C/span\u003E();\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E service.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EAddStudent\u003C/span\u003E(student);\n    broker.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EVerifyInsert\u003C/span\u003E(student);\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STXTEST005\u003C/span\u003E\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E]\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Easync\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldAddStudent\u003C/span\u003E()\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// given\u003C/span\u003E\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E student = \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003ECreateStudent\u003C/span\u003E();\n\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// when\u003C/span\u003E\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E service.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EAddStudent\u003C/span\u003E(student);\n\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// then\u003C/span\u003E\n    broker.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EVerifyInsert\u003C/span\u003E(student);\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
  ],
